WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.688
Last, turn findings into a program.

2
00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:05.025
Read each result before counting it.

3
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:07.178
Only ScubaGear's Fail and Warning,

4
00:00:07.178 --> 00:00:11.562
and the Zero Trust Assessment's
Failed and Investigate, are findings.

5
00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:14.562
A skipped check isn't
a gap and isn't a pass.

6
00:00:14.562 --> 00:00:18.414
It's absence of evidence, recorded
with the reason, which is often a

7
00:00:18.414 --> 00:00:22.837
license or a government-cloud feature
that isn't available in the boundary.

8
00:00:22.837 --> 00:00:28.542
The program scores findings with a
documented method: severity from 0 to 100,

9
00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:31.530
priority as severity divided by effort,

10
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.700
and buckets from P1 at
50 or above down to P4.

11
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.466
Quick wins go into the next change window;

12
00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:40.638
major projects go onto a
pillar owner's roadmap.

13
00:00:40.638 --> 00:00:47.037
Both tools' findings are reconciled
against the same SP 800-53 control,

14
00:00:47.037 --> 00:00:50.413
so two pieces of evidence become
one finding for one owner.

15
00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:55.233
Anything not fixed and not excepted becomes
a plan of action and milestones item,

16
00:00:55.233 --> 00:00:57.751
which the authorizing official approves.

17
00:00:57.751 --> 00:01:01.749
Drift between intervals goes to
the authorizing official too,

18
00:01:01.749 --> 00:01:03.825
not only to security operations.

19
00:01:03.825 --> 00:01:06.655
And re-run after every remediation wave,

20
00:01:06.655 --> 00:01:10.660
so a finding is closed by
evidence, not by a ticket status.
